Third-party components and data
-------------------------------

vidyut (vidyut-prakriya, vidyut-kosha, vidyut-lipi, vidyut-chandas) by the Ambuda project,
https://github.com/ambuda-org/vidyut. Licensed under the MIT License. vidyut is used as a
library. Its linguistic data is downloaded at run time and is not redistributed in this
repository.

Digital Corpus of Sanskrit (DCS) by Oliver Hellwig, https://github.com/OliverHellwig/sanskrit.
Licensed under CC BY 4.0. Citation: Hellwig, Oliver (2010–2024): The Digital Corpus of Sanskrit
(DCS). The file mayur/gold/ramayana_bala_1.json is an excerpt converted from the DCS CoNLL-U
files (Rāmāyaṇa, Bālakāṇḍa 1), transliterated to Devanagari. The following files are derived
from DCS annotations and carry the same attribution: the trained model files in mayur/models/
(statistics of DCS annotations), the sampled verses in eval/samples/dev*.json, the word splits
and morphology inside eval/review/claude/*.json, and mayur/gold/pools.json (chapter ids).
Frequency tables and DCS-derived gloss tables are built locally by script and are not committed.

Universal Dependencies treebanks UD_Sanskrit-UFAL and UD_Sanskrit-Vedic, licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0, are fetched by scripts/fetch_gold_external.py for evaluation only and are not
redistributed in this repository.

Annotations written by Claude (a large language model by Anthropic) during development, not
human-verified, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0: the gloss draft table mayur/annotations/gloss_draft.json,
the suffix-sense table mayur/annotations/suffix_senses.json, the table of root meanings by class
mayur/annotations/gloss_roots.json, and the roles, compound types,
prose order and English in eval/review/claude/. The interpreter itself uses no language model
at run time.

Monier-Williams Sanskrit-English Dictionary, Cologne Digital Sanskrit Dictionaries,
https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de. The licence is unclear. The dictionary may optionally
be fetched by script for local use only. It is never committed or redistributed in this
repository.

No glosses or translations were copied from valmiki.iitk.ac.in or valmikiramayan.net.
